            <ArticleTitle>Traumatic aortic dissection and coronary fistula treated with transcatheter management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1013-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An adolescent male presented with a dissection of the thoracic aorta and a left anterior descending coronary artery to right ventricular fistula following a road traffic accident. Authors report the management of this patient using a transcatheter approach for both these arterial issues, with stenting to the thoracic aorta and coil embolization of the coronary artery to right ventricular fistula as a staged procedure, along with a brief review of the literature on traumatic arterial injuries.</AbstractText>
